---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy — Egemen Özen" description="Privacy information for Egemen Özen's personal portfolio.">
  <section class="case-hero" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
    <div class="container">
      <a class="text-link case-home-link" href="/">← Home</a>
      <div class="section-label">Privacy</div>
      <h1 id="privacy-title">Privacy information</h1>
      <p class="case-subtitle">This notice describes the data handling relevant to this static portfolio.</p>
      <div class="case-body">
        <section class="case-detail" aria-labelledby="controller-title">
          <h2 id="controller-title">Controller and contact</h2>
          <p>Egemen Özen is responsible for this portfolio. For privacy questions, contact <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="case-detail" aria-labelledby="hosting-title">
          <h2 id="hosting-title">Hosting and technical access data</h2>
          <p>This static website is hosted by GitHub Pages, a service provided by GitHub. GitHub states that visitors' IP addresses are logged and stored for security purposes. This is technical access logging handled by the hosting service; the site itself has no account, visitor database or analytics dashboard. See <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/what-is-github-pages" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub's GitHub Pages documentation</a> and <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub's Privacy Statement</a> for the provider's information about its processing.</p>
          <p>The portfolio contains no analytics, advertising trackers, contact forms or embedded third-party content, and it does not set site cookies. External links, including project demos and source repositories, open services governed by their own privacy notices. Following the email link opens the visitor's configured email application; this website does not receive the message through a form.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="case-detail" aria-labelledby="purpose-title">
          <h2 id="purpose-title">Purpose and legal basis</h2>
          <p>GitHub describes security as the purpose of its Pages visitor-IP logging and provides its own Privacy Statement for details. If you email Egemen Özen, your address and message are used to respond. For a work-related enquiry, the legal basis may be taking steps at your request before a contract under Article 6(1)(b) GDPR; for other enquiries, it may be the legitimate interest in responding under Article 6(1)(f). The appropriate basis depends on the specific message.</p>
          <p>Email correspondence is retained only for as long as needed to handle the enquiry and any applicable legal obligations. No specific log retention period is stated here because GitHub's public GitHub Pages documentation does not specify one. Please consult GitHub's Privacy Statement for information about the hosting provider's handling and retention.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="case-detail" aria-labelledby="rights-title">
          <h2 id="rights-title">Your rights</h2>
          <p>Where the GDPR applies, you may have rights to access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection and data portability, subject to the applicable conditions. You may also lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority. For requests concerning information you sent directly to Egemen Özen, use the email address above. Requests about GitHub's own hosting logs should be directed to GitHub.</p>
        </section>
        <p class="case-scope">Last updated: 27 October 2026.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
